From: Gezim <25499045+gezimos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: the lockscreen measures notifications collapsed

0054 hides a lockscreen notification that does not fit whole, since there
is no shelf to take it. It measured each row with getMaxAllowedChildHeight,
the intrinsic height, which for a bundle (a group summary with children,
as the Google app posts its weather) includes the children. The lockscreen
draws every row collapsed, and NotificationStackSizeCalculator counts them
collapsed (getMinHeight), so it allowed the bundle while this check hid it:
a weather notification under any other one never showed, though there was
room for it. The check now measures with getMinHeight as the counter does.
---
 .../statusbar/notification/stack/StackScrollAlgorithm.java     | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/notification/stack/StackScrollAlgorithm.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/notification/stack/StackScrollAlgorithm.java
index 5bbf076..db38ac9 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/notification/stack/StackScrollAlgorithm.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/notification/stack/StackScrollAlgorithm.java
@@ -816,8 +816,9 @@ public class StackScrollAlgorithm {
                     }
                     // Kompakt: on the lockscreen a notification that does not fit whole is
                     // hidden, not left as a sliver above the shelf (which is not drawn there).
+                    // Measured collapsed, as NotificationStackSizeCalculator counts it.
                     if (ambientState.isOnKeyguard() && !viewState.hidden && !view.isPinned()
-                            && viewState.getYTranslation() + getMaxAllowedChildHeight(view)
+                            && viewState.getYTranslation() + view.getMinHeight(true)
                                     > shelfStart) {
                         viewState.hidden = true;
                         viewState.inShelf = true;
